The backend for future.apply is the future package. Check its documentation. In theory, future uses some black magic to detect which variables, functions and packages you use to run the parallel part and automatically exports those to the workers independently of the backend, even in Windows (still C++ objects such as the simmer environment won't work). Sometimes it fails to do so, and you have a mechanism better than doParallel to define those dependencies.

Iñaki

